# DO NOT PUSH TO STAGING UNLESS
1. Robert says **pts** (push to staging), OR
2. Robert says "push to staging", OR
3. You have more than 10 updates to make in a session.
Otherwise: commit locally only. No push. (Vercel build fees.)

# SHORTHANDS
- **pts** = Push to staging. When Robert says "pts", commit and push to `origin/staging`.
- **ptm** = Push to main. When Robert says "ptm", run `npm run merge-to-main` (merge staging → main, exclude internal docs, push main, purge Vercel cache). Do not touch main without ptm.

---

# REMEMBER

- **Two branches, one Supabase.** We have `staging` and `main` (Git). There is one Supabase project. Both deploy to the same Supabase.
- **Pushing to staging** happens only when Robert says **pts** or "push to staging" or when there are more than 10 updates. Otherwise do not push (Vercel build fees). Approval for `main` requires **ptm** or "push to main"; use `npm run merge-to-main`.

---

# Branch Flow (Locked)

**Deployment direction is one-way only:**

- **Allowed:** `staging` → `main` (merge or deploy from staging to production).
- **Forbidden:** Never merge or deploy `main` into `staging`. Never bring main back into staging.

**Internal documents are excluded from main.** Run `npm run merge-to-main` (not a manual merge). This script merges staging into main, removes paths in `scripts/internal-documents.txt` from main, pushes to origin, then purges Vercel CDN and Data cache (via `VERCEL_TOKEN` in `.env`). Those files remain on staging only and never appear on the public production branch.

---

# Admin never on production (main)

**Admin login and all /admin/* routes must not be reachable on production.**

- **Vercel:** `vercel.json` redirects `/admin` and `/admin/:path*` to `/404` when host is `www.top10lists.us` or `top10lists.us` (production only).
- **React:** `AdminRouteGuard` blocks production hosts so admin UI never renders there.

---

# How to push

- **pts** or **"push to staging":** Push to staging. Stage, commit, `git push origin staging`.
- **ptm** or **"push to main":** Run `npm run merge-to-main` only; no manual merge.

**When you push to staging:** `git add ...`, `git commit -m "message"`, `git push origin staging`.
